      "side": 1,
      "message": "In the context of \"Should the BUILD file appear in the workspace\", I dont have a strong opinion, but perhaps +cparsons has an opinion?\n\nThe current implementation does have a side effect on `TransformSubpackagePaths`. In the above example at ToT, if we have a target in $TOP/BUILD that depends on a .cpp file in b/b.cpp, then its bp2build generated target will be\n\n```\n# ToT\ncc_library (\n  srcs \u003d [\":b/b.cpp\"], # does not build\n)\n```\n\nAnd after this CL\n```\ncc_library (\n  srcs \u003d [\"//b:b.cpp\"], # builds successfully\n)\n```\n\nI would like to propose that we submit this fix for `TransformSubpackagePaths`. Once we have clarity on what the expected behavior for symlink is, we can drop this special handling.",
